<title>USA: Gillette, Duracell in $7 billion merger.</title>
<headline>Gillette, Duracell in $7 billion merger.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer products manufacturer Gillette Co. and battery maker Duracell International Inc. Thursday announced a $7 billion merger.</p>
<p>The deal values Duracell's stock at 0.904 share of Gillette, or $58.85 per share, they said.</p>
<p>Gillette said it will issue about 108 million primary shares in the stock transaction, putting the value at about $7 billion.</p>
</text>
